				\begin{document}$$y \in \left\{\mathrm{0,1}\right\}$$\end{document}y∈0,1. If y equals one, it denotes churn; otherwise, it represents non-churn. Our goal is to create a model that can accurately distinguish churn and non-churn based on the training data and class labels we provided.

The pattern evaluation in the forward LSTM occurs from left to right by processing two inputs, the current "kt" and the preceding input "kt−1." The forward LSTM generates the corresponding output sequence \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
