The size of the feature map (Y) is reduced by using the maxpool layer, which selects the most significant features (maximum value). By removing non-maximal (less significant) attributes, this approach aids in optimizing computation time. The following is how the maxpool procedure is carried out:15\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
